    "granted_by": "Maintainer decision, 2026-08-22. 'GO for Recovery Continuation Attempt 4. The Attempt-3 blocker is closed sufficiently for another paid continuation. I reviewed d592b8a: the scratch fallback is portable, HF_TOKEN correctly covers the pod environment with the local token file retained only as fallback, and the canonical-shard test rewrite preserves the actual drift refusal rather than weakening it. The targeted pod-like regression is the right closure. No TEST_IGNORES exemption or generic readiness guard is needed.' Against last tested implementation d592b8a, which is also the pre-authorization HEAD. Since attempt 3 exactly one closure landed and was accepted: PORTABILITY OF THE LEAF PUBLISHER. Attempt 3 reached the pod's setup CPU test gate and failed it because scripts/autoinit/publish_selected_leaves.py hard-coded dev-box paths, and although that module is a dev-box publishing tool the paid session never executes, its TEST module is part of the suite the pod gate runs. Three independent host dependencies were found and closed: verify() called tempfile.mkdtemp with dir='/home/ecs-user/aad-scratch', now scratch_dir() returning the configured AAD_SCRATCH if it names an existing directory, else the dev-box root if present, else None so tempfile chooses; token() read '~/.cache/huggingface/token', which no pod has, now reading HF_TOKEN first with the file retained as fallback -- this one was invisible until mkdtemp stopped failing first, because it is evaluated as an argument to hf_hub_download and therefore runs even in tests that patch the download away; and test_the_before_manifest_refuses_a_drifted_canonical_shard drove build_before() against the real 5.55 GiB canonical store, so on any pod it exited at 'canonical leaf missing' and the drift assertion never executed, now driven against a synthetic store and record. No TEST_IGNORES entry and no generic hard-coded-host-root guard were added, as instructed. Verified at $0 on the current tree: full suite 2162 passed / 12 skipped, +2 on the 2160 baseline with the skip count unchanged; the publisher module 11 passed on a POD-LIKE HOST with no aad-scratch, no aad-artifacts and no token file, HF_TOKEN set as a pod sets it; frozen-asset verifier passed with no problems; 6 mutations each turning a passing state into a failing one, including deleting the drift check to prove the rewritten test was not weakened. The continuation harness digest is UNCHANGED at 162c09ed because the publisher and its tests are outside the 22-file set, so the repair moved the session commit and nothing else.\n\nCovers: One (1) launch of the AutoInitializer Phase-A RECOVERY CONTINUATION, attempt 4, on a single NVIDIA L40S at no more than $0.99/h. It imports the verified Attempt-12 Stage-1 result -- the five preserved selected leaves, in the committed selected order, re-identified from the bytes that actually arrive on the pod -- and runs recovery Stages 2 through 5 under the frozen science, the existing watchdog, soft-stop, hard-stop, artifact-gate and provider-confirmed teardown behaviour. The reviewed execution path is preserved exactly: Stage 0 attestation, strict Stage-1 import, canonical-control measurement once on the frozen Stage-1 suite, admit_leaves over the five imported leaves plus the measured control, device handoff and headroom gate, then frozen recovery Stages 2-5 only, with the conditional seed-sc rung firing only if the frozen rule fires. The five leaves travel as 15 relay inputs from the private transport repository, a path already PROVEN on paid hardware by attempt 3, which reached ASSETS_STAGED, ASSETS_READY and VLLM_READY; only 2 small artifacts totalling 1.577 MiB remain on the scp path. Authorized pricing is DERIVED from continuation_budget(), not written: expected $14.9233, per-launch hard ceiling $16.7456, which is also the hard cap. The beam search is not run, not reconstructed, and is structurally unreachable from this harness.\n\nCumulative spend at approval $213.